(Medication Safety: The Five Rights) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every medication administration should satisfy five checks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Right patient - confirm identity before giving any drug.) Tj
T*
(2. Right drug - read the label, not the box shape or color.) Tj
T*
(3. Right dose - calculate and double check, especially for children.) Tj
T*
(4. Right route - oral, topical and inhaled forms are not interchangeable.) Tj
T*
(5. Right time - follow the prescribed interval, not convenience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Look-alike and sound-alike drug names are a major source of error.) Tj
T*
(Store high-risk medicines separately and label them clearly.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
