50 750 Td
(Storage, Disposal and When to Seek Help) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Storage:) Tj
T*
(Keep medicines dry and away from direct sunlight. Most products are stable) Tj
T*
(between 10 and 30 degrees Celsius. A few require refrigeration at 2 to 8) Tj
T*
(degrees Celsius and must never be frozen. Keep the original packaging and) Tj
T*
(leaflet so the expiry date and ingredients stay available.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Disposal:) Tj
T*
(Do not flush unused medicines down the drain. Return them to a pharmacy) Tj
T*
(collection point. Never keep expired tablets for a rainy day.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Seek immediate medical help if a person shows difficult breathing, swelling) Tj
T*
(of the face or throat, widespread rash, or loss of consciousness after taking) Tj
T*
(any medicine. These may indicate a serious allergic reaction.) Tj
ET
endstream
